            "topic": "Supabase client handling",
            "choice": "One auth-owned getRequestSession() returning actor and cookie client together; the privileged service-role factory is untouched.",
            "rationale": "Cookie-scoped and privileged clients must not sit behind one ambiguous factory, and a caller-supplied actor must never be paired with an independently created client."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Authorization layers",
            "choice": "Authenticate at every channel; enforce tenant/ownership predicates in the store and mirror them in RLS. No business-policy module.",
            "rationale": "The task specifies only authentication plus tenant ownership; inventing role policy would be future policy the product does not require. Layouts, middleware and hidden UI authorize nothing."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Failure carriers",
            "choice": "Typed values for validation/unauthorized/conflict/not_found; exceptions for defects and outages; one report per channel.",
            "rationale": "Channel-native outcomes over one universal wrapper, with the adapter translating provider codes and the outer channel owning the single report and the safe public body."
